      "title": "nettrace_3gpp_32_423: accept rawMsg packet without any payload",
      "message": "nettrace_3gpp_32_423: accept rawMsg packet without any payload\n\nEven if 3GPP 32.423 mandates to have a payload for the rawMsg field (at\nleast af far as I understand the spec) it seems like some tools do not always\ninsert it. While I do not see the use case for this, it's quite easy to\nworkaround.\n\nFixes #20825\n",
      "author_name": "Pascal Quantin",
      "author_email": "pascal@wireshark.org",
      "authored_date": "2025-11-06T14:43:24.000+01:00",
